message: "If you use or implement SILT Core v0.2, please cite this release."
title: "SILT Core v0.2: Semantic Architecture"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: 2026-09-23
authors:
  - family-names: "Farry"
    given-names: "Gareth"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sugarlicks/silt-identity-core"
url: "https://siltcore.org"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22908026"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
type: software
abstract: >-
  SILT Core is a semantic architecture for moments of encounter between
  participants and systems grounded in different legal, customary, cultural,
  private, institutional or technical orders. Its canonical seam is Source to
  Standing to Presentation to evaluation at the encounter. SILT enables
  relevant relational legitimacy to become mutually legible without requiring
  originating orders to collapse into a single ontology or surrender their own
  sources of authority.
keywords:
  - semantic interoperability
  - digital identity
  - plural legal orders
  - Indigenous data governance
  - authority
  - standing
  - AI agents
  - private ordering
